WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.609
The key ablation varies only how the recurrent
weight is parameterized,

00:00:04.689 --> 00:00:06.524
holding initialization fixed.

00:00:06.604 --> 00:00:12.005
On MNIST, the three stable reparameterizations,
softplus, exponential, and inverse,

00:00:12.085 --> 00:00:16.826
all speed up optimization and reach higher test
accuracy than the direct,

00:00:16.906 --> 00:00:20.590
unstable parameterization where the weight is used as-is.

00:00:20.670 --> 00:00:26.138
Importantly, since reparameterization does not
change the model's inherent capacity,

00:00:26.218 --> 00:00:30.034
the final performance across stable variants is
comparable,

00:00:30.114 --> 00:00:36.109
isolating the effect as an optimization and
stability benefit rather than a capacity change.

00:00:36.189 --> 00:00:37.562
On the synthetic side,

00:00:37.642 --> 00:00:44.100
applying exponential and softplus
reparameterizations to linear RNNs approximating polynomial-decay

00:00:44.180 --> 00:00:48.195
targets restores the expected continuous limiting
error curve,

00:00:48.275 --> 00:00:50.440
confirming stability is recovered.
